# f1 = run. Nothing in the loop writes what `o.size` reads, so the read stands in front of the loop, rightly. Where proofs are checked at run time (testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime, which --aot-harden=proof-checks stands for) an answer
# that comes from in front of a loop is read again in the turn and compared, BUT ONLY WHAT MAY BE RUN AGAIN UNSEEN IS READ AGAIN (under-the-word-a-getter-copied-in-line-in-the-head-of-a-loop-runs-once-a-turn.ir). `o.size` is a form
# of a built-in: the bound of its operation has to allow for every built-in and says that it may run code; this one only reads. For a form of a built-in the exact effects decide. Under a lie that a callee in the loop writes nothing
# (a fact ends in a callee that is said to write nothing: the size of a map) the process then ends by name; the lies that the tree can lay take one part of one row and do not carry this read out.
